# Instructor-only / answer-key material for live scenarios — these spell out
# exact lab credentials, full step-by-step attack procedures, Wazuh rule
# internals, and the AP role's hardware bring-up details. They're prep
# material for whoever is presenting, not something to ship in a repo
# students/attendees (or the public) can browse — keeping them out of the
# commit is the whole point, not an oversight. Stays on disk locally; just
# never tracked. Grouped under docs/labs/wifi/ (walkthroughs, presenter
# guide, slide content/deck/titles, study content, hardware notes, assets)
# so this is one pattern instead of a dozen.
docs/labs/wifi/
docs/labs/ransomware-intrusion.md
docs/labs/malware-triage.md
